              ],
              "start": 0,
              "end": 76,
              "quote": "中国古典文学在中国的文化肌理中占有重要地位。这些文学瑰宝植根于数千年的历史，传达着中国思想的精髓，为了解世界上最古老的文明之一的文化变迁提供了一扇窗口。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:2",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:2"
              ],
              "start": 77,
              "end": 208,
              "quote": "中国古典文学就像一个百宝箱，装满了智慧、良言和深刻的思想。儒家经典，如《论语》和《孟子》，就像重要的基石，长久以来帮助确立了中国人应当如何为人处世的规范。诗歌，尤其是李白等唐代诗人的诗作，就像永恒的歌，诗人借助它们表达中国人对生活、自然的感受以及他们强烈的情感。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:3",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:3"
              ],
              "start": 209,
              "end": 277,
              "quote": "古典文学就像一部讲述朝代更替的大型史书。《史记》和《三国演义》等书不只是故事，更是一扇扇特别的窗口，让我们看到那个时代许多人所经历的事。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:4",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:4"
              ],
              "start": 278,
              "end": 378,
              "quote": "在一个快速变化的世界里，中国古典文学就像一块文化基石，增进了中国人的联结感和认同感。它的特别之处在于它不会过时。这使它成为一个绝佳的媒介，让不同代际的人都能与构成中国人思维方式的价值观和梦想紧密相连。"
            }
          ]
        },
        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:1",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:1",
            "text": "Chinese classical literature holds a vital position in the cultural fabric of China. Rooted in a history extending for thousands of years, these literary treasures convey the core of Chinese thought, providing a window into the cultural transition of one of the world’s oldest civilizations."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "Chinese classical literature is like a treasure chest filled with wisdom, good advice, and deep thoughts. The Confucian classics, such as The Analects and Mencius, are like the important building blocks that have helped create the rules for how people should behave in China for a very long time. The poems, particularly those by Tang poets like Li Bai, are like timeless songs, through which the poets express the Chinese feelings towards life, nature, and their intense emotions."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "Classical literature is like a large history book that narrates the transition of dynasties. Books like Records of the Grand Historian and Romance of the Three Kingdoms are not just stories, but special windows that let us see what many people were experiencing/experienced during those times."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-tangshan-2025-01:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "In a rapidly changing world, Chinese classical literature is like a cultural cornerstone, encouraging a sense of connection and identity for the Chinese people. The special thing about it is that it doesn’t get old. This makes it a great medium for different generations to feel a strong link to the values and dreams that make up the Chinese way of thinking."
          }
        ],
